# --- starlette — transitive via `fastapi ~= 0.115.0` -------------
#
# 3 findings ({'HIGH': 3}), installed 0.46.2.
# Not directly pinned. Reaching starlette >= 0.49.1 requires a fastapi bump
# outside the declared compatible-release range. Two of the three are
# StaticFiles/Range-header issues on surfaces this template does not mount
# (no StaticFiles, no Range handling); the third is a form-parsing DoS that
# does apply to `/predict` under a hostile client.
#
# Review question: does the pinned fastapi range now reach a fixed
# starlette? That is a one-line check and the cheapest of the three to close.
#
# expiry: 2026-12-08  reason: starlette 0.46.2 -> needs 0.49.1 (major bump); HIGH
CVE-2025-62727
# expiry: 2026-12-08  reason: starlette 0.46.2 -> needs 1.1.0 (major bump); HIGH
CVE-2026-48818
# expiry: 2026-12-08  reason: starlette 0.46.2 -> needs 1.3.1 (major bump); HIGH
CVE-2026-54283

# --- pyarrow — pinned `~= 18.0.0` for the parquet prediction log (ADR-006)
#
# 1 findings ({'HIGH': 1}), installed 18.0.0.
# A use-after-free DoS in the Arrow C++ layer. The template's exposure is the
# prediction logger writing parquet it produced itself, not parsing
# attacker-supplied Arrow data, which is the vector the advisory describes.
#
# Review question: does anything now READ third-party parquet? If so this
# acceptance is void and the bump becomes urgent.
#
# expiry: 2026-12-08  reason: pyarrow 18.0.0 -> needs 23.0.1 (major bump); HIGH
CVE-2026-25087
